{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) is requesting implementation of srd058-rm requirements R2.1 through R2.4 in the go-unix-utils project. This is a \"stitch\" task (task #5404) from the cobbler code generation pipeline. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: `-r`/`-R`/`--recursive` must remove directories and their contents recursively\n   - R2.2: `-f`/`--force` must ignore non-existent files and never prompt, overriding `-i` and `-I`\n   - R2.3: When `-r` and `-f` are combined, must silently remove directory trees without prompting\n   - R2.4: `-d`/`--dir` must remove empty directories; without `-d` or `-r`, directory removal fails\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/rm/main.go` and `cmd/rm/rm_test.go`. Acceptance criteria require compilation, vet, and test passage.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against `grm` (GNU rm from Homebrew)\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for building the Go binary under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"grm\")` with `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment variable for deterministic output comparison\n   - `os.RemoveAll()` for recursive directory removal in Go\n   - `os.Remove()` for removing individual files and empty directories\n   - Flag parsing: `-f` overrides `-i`/`-I`; `-i` overrides `-f`; last flag wins pattern\n   - The `interactiveMode` typed enum (iota): `interactiveNever`, `interactiveOnce`, `interactiveAlways`\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - E8 constitution rule: no function may exceed 40 lines\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd058-rm.yaml** (read, not to be modified)\n     - Contains full SRD with R1-R4 requirement groups\n     - R2 group (our target): recursive removal, force mode, combined -rf, empty dir removal\n     - Non-goals: no --one-file-system, no --preserve-root/--no-preserve-root, no shred\n     \n   - **cmd/rm/main.go** (to be modified)\n     - Already has complete flag parsing for all R2 flags (-r, -R, --recursive, -f, --force, -d, --dir)\n     - `options` struct already has `recursive`, `force`, `dir` boolean fields\n     - `removePath()` already branches on `opts.recursive` and `opts.dir` but delegates to stub functions\n     - **STUB: `removeDir()`** at line 163-165 returns `fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")` — needs recursive removal implementation\n     - **STUB: `removeEmptyDir()`** at line 167-169 returns `fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")` — needs empty directory removal\n     - `removeFile()` at line 159-161 only calls `os.Remove(path)` — may need verbose output support\n     - Force mode for non-existent files already handled in `removePath()` lines 128-131\n     - Key existing helper: `isDotOrDotDot()`, `sysErrMsg()`, `errnoMsg()`\n     ```go\n     func removeDir(path string, opts options) error {\n         return fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")\n     }\n     \n     func removeEmptyDir(path string, opts options) error {\n         return fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/rm/rm_test.go** (to be modified)\n     - Has `TestDiff` function with existing subtests for R1.1-R1.4 scenarios\n     - Uses two testing patterns: `testutils.RunDiffTests` and custom `runRemovalTest`/`runBin`/`compareResults` helpers\n     - `normalizeBinaryName` regex: `(/\\S+/)?g?rm\\b` replaces binary name paths with \"rm\"\n     - `runBin()` helper runs binary with context timeout, captures stdout/stderr/exitCode\n     - `compareResults()` compares normalized outputs between Go and reference binary\n     - Existing tests cover: dot rejection, dotdot rejection, nonexistent file, directory without -r, single file, multiple files, partial failure, file and directory without -r\n     ```go\n     func runRemovalTest(t *testing.T, goBin, refBin string, args []string, setup func(string)) {\n         t.Helper()\n         goDir := t.TempDir()\n         refDir := t.TempDir()\n         setup(goDir)\n         setup(refDir)\n         goRes := runBin(t, goBin, args, goDir)\n         refRes := runBin(t, refBin, args, refDir)\n         compareResults(t, args, goRes, refRes)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/** (referenced, not to be modified)\n     - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` \n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles from within module\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — I only completed the file reading phase before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing code already has the flag parsing and routing logic in place; the core work is implementing the two stub functions (`removeDir` and `removeEmptyDir`) and adding verbose output support\n   - `removeDir` needs to walk directory contents recursively, remove files and subdirectories, handle verbose output, and handle the dot/dotdot check (already in removePath)\n   - `removeEmptyDir` needs to attempt `os.Remove()` on the directory (which succeeds only for empty dirs)\n   - Need to add verbose printing (`fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"removed '%s'\\n\", path)` or stdout — need to check GNU rm behavior, likely stdout)\n   - Need to add test cases for: -r recursive removal, -f force on nonexistent, -rf combined, -d empty directory, -d non-empty directory failure, -v verbose output\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The full stitch task description with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution,